sis" 1556 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042225/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-130868" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following matrices are transformed into the $2\\times 2$ identity matrix after applying the row operations ${R}_{1}↔{R}_{2}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1}?$\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042225/state.json" "file_sha256" "5a694d44f432abaff4cfb88d174cecf20a51952c9d7ff76670960cd9ecaab98b" "basis" 1556 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042225/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-130868" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's apply the operations to each of the matrices:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & \\ne I,\\,\\times  \\\\ B & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =I\\,✓ \\\\ C & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & \\ne I,\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$B$ only\"." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042225/state.json" "file_sha256" "5a694d44f432abaff4cfb88d174cecf20a51952c9d7ff76670960cd9ecaab98b" "basis" 1556 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042225/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-130868" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042225/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7bbd11558f95d5c63611e864d4e4f9e2d18f6764e1cd0e12fd343d300266d8e9" "basis" 1556 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042225/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-130868" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042225/state.json" "file_sha256" "5a694d44f432abaff4cfb88d174cecf20a51952c9d7ff76670960cd9ecaab98b" "basis" 1556 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042225/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-130868" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "$A$ and $B$ only"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042225/state.json" "file_sha256" "5a694d44f432abaff4cfb88d174cecf20a51952c9d7ff76670960cd9ecaab98b" "basis" 1556 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042225/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-130868" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "$A$ only"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/re