ure-workers/linear/14042225/state.json" "file_sha256" "5a694d44f432abaff4cfb88d174cecf20a51952c9d7ff76670960cd9ecaab98b" "basis" 1556 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042225/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-43004" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The inverse of the matrix $V$ is found using row operations, as shown below. What are the row operations corresponding to each step?\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[V\\,|\\,I\\,] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] &  & \\text{___________} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & \\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}] &  & \\text{___________} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 & -\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & \\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042225/state.json" "file_sha256" "5a694d44f432abaff4cfb88d174cecf20a51952c9d7ff76670960cd9ecaab98b" "basis" 1556 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042225/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-43004" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We write down $V$ and the identity matrix $I$ side-by-side (as shown below) and apply the standard Gauss-Jordan method to transform the matrix $V$ into the identity matrix. We perform the same row operations on both matrices:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[V\\,|\\,I\\,] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & \\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+(-1){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 & -\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & \\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding row operations are\n\n$$\n{R}_{2}:=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{2},\\,{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+(-1){R}_{2}.\n$$\n\nThe matrix ${V}^{-1}$ is given by the right-hand side of our big matrix after all of the transformations have been completed. Therefore, \n\n$$\n{V}^{-1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042225/state.json" "file_sha256" "5a694d44f432abaff4cfb88d174cecf20a51952c9d7ff76670960cd9ecaab98b" "basis" 1556 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042225/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-43004" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042225/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7bbd11558f95d5c63611e864d4e4f9e2d18f6764e1cd0e12fd343d300266d8e9" "basis" 1556 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042225/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-43004" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042225/state.json" "file_sha256" "5a694d44f432abaff4cfb88d174cecf20a51952c9d7ff76670960cd9ecaab98b" "basis" 1556 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042225/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-43004" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "{R}_{1}:=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1},\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{1}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042225/state.json" "file_sha256" "5a694d44f432abaff4cfb88d174cecf20a51952c9d7ff7667096