b6345aea8f1ec84430e09e2c77b98a2f1e0bb7be114e09fdd2b9751eea72"} {"question" "q-31945" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We write down $K$ and the identity matrix $I$ side-by-side (as shown below) and apply the standard Gauss-Jordan method to transform the matrix $K$ into the identity matrix. We perform the same row operations on both matrices:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[K\\,|\\,I] & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 4 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 3 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=-\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -\\frac{4}{3} & -\\frac{1}{3} & 0 \\\\ -2 & 3 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -\\frac{4}{3} & -\\frac{1}{3} & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{3} & -\\frac{2}{3} & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=3{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -\\frac{4}{3} & -\\frac{1}{3} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & 3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+\\frac{4}{3}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding row operations are\n\n$$\n{R}_{1}:=-\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{1},\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1},\\,{R}_{2}:=3{R}_{2},\\,{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+\\frac{4}{3}{R}_{2}.\n$$\n\nThe matrix ${K}^{-1}$ is given by the right-hand side of our big matrix after all of the transformations have been completed. Therefore, \n\n$$\n{K}^{-1}=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 4 \\\\ -2 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14080619/state.json" "file_sha256" "b540b6345aea8f1ec84430e09e2c77b98a2f1e0bb7be114e09fdd2b9751eea72"} {"question" "q-31945" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14080619/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a8001d243f786fcf7dc29b56b9689ddd6ffa0ca0841dedb27f7c113350df4c16"} {"question" "q-31945" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answe