1} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & \\frac{1}{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+(-3){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & \\frac{1}{2} & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding row operations are\n\n$$\nR_1 := \\dfrac{1}{2}R_1,\n\\qquad\nR_1 := R_1+(-3)R_2.\n$$\n\nThe matrix $A^{-1}$ is given by the right-hand side of our big matrix after all of the transformations have been completed. Therefore, \n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042225/assets/694b10f1d1c18f25e079e9e7cc75e9cc457ef01d0c229f006308fd667108459b.png)"]] "immutable_answers" [17592186113950 17592186113951 17592186113952 17592186113953 17592186113954 17592186113956 17592186113957 17592186113958 17592186113959 17592186113960 17592186316047 17592186316048 17592186316049 17592186316050 17592186316051 17592186316054 17592186316055 17592186316056 17592186316057 17592186316058 17592186316061 17592186316062 17592186316063 17592186316064 17592186316065 17592186316082 17592186316083 17592186316084 17592186316085 17592186316086 17592186316116 17592186316117 17592186316118 17592186316119 17592186316120 17592186316123 17592186316124 17592186316125 17592186316126 17592186316127] "immutable_fields" [[17592186113949 :answer-field/correct] [17592186113949 :answer-field/id] [17592186113949 :answer-field/key] [17592186113949 :answer-field/type] [17592186113955 :answer-field/correct] [17592186113955 :answer-field/id] [17592186113955 :answer-field/key] [17592186113955 :answer-field/type] [17592186316046 :answer-field/correct] [17592186316046 :answer-field/id] [17592186316046 :answer-field/key] [17592186316046 :answer-field/type] [17592186316053 :answer-field/correct] [17592186316053 :answer-field/id] [17592186316053 :answer-field/key] [17592186316053 :answer-field/type] [17592186316060 :answer-field/correct] [17592186316060 :answer-field/id] [17592186316060 :answer-field/